How it is used:
  - As a Go module dependency, unmodified (pinned in go.mod and go.sum):
    pkg/tap, pkg/services/dhcp, pkg/services/forwarder (the UDP proxy),
    pkg/transport and pkg/types.
  - Adapted into this module. These files carry the Apache-2.0 header and a
    "MODIFIED" note that says what changed:
      internal/gateway/gateway.go  from pkg/virtualnetwork/virtualnetwork.go
                                   and pkg/virtualnetwork/services.go
      internal/gateway/forward.go  from pkg/services/forwarder/tcp.go, udp.go
                                   and udp_proxy.go

It also depends on gVisor (https://gvisor.dev, Apache-2.0), miekg/dns
(BSD-3-Clause), inetaf/tcpproxy (Apache-2.0), sirupsen/logrus (MIT),
insomniacslk/dhcp (BSD-3-Clause) and golang.org/x modules (BSD-3-Clause);
their licenses are in the Go module cache entries go.sum pins.

